1
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:24,260
They're two best friends, a million miles from home. On an incredible adventure,
beyond the boundaries of space and time. In a place called...

2
00:08:36,521 --> 00:08:42,521
Mio in the Land of Faraway is a adventure, drama, fantasy
film directed by Vladimir Grammatikov.

3
00:12:54,782 --> 00:13:00,782
Under the watch of his unkind realtives, lonely Bosse's luck is changed when
he is sent to the land where his real father is the King.

4
00:17:13,043 --> 00:17:19,043
In that country, he sets out on a quest, together with his
new friend, to destroy the evil Knight Kato.

5
00:21:31,304 --> 00:21:37,304
Mio / Bosse, played by Nick Pickard.

6
00:25:49,565 --> 00:25:55,565
Jum-Jum / Benke, played by Christian Bale.

7
00:30:07,826 --> 00:30:13,826
The King, played by Timothy Bottoms.

8
00:34:26,086 --> 00:34:32,086
Kato, played by Christopher Lee.

9
00:38:44,347 --> 00:38:50,347
The Weaver Woman, played by Susannah York.

10
00:43:02,608 --> 00:43:08,608
The Swordmaker, played by Sverre Anker Ousdal.

11
00:47:20,869 --> 00:47:26,869
Mio in the Land of Faraway (Swedish: Mio min Mio; Russian: Мио, мой Мио, romanized: Mio, moy Mio) is a 1987 fantasy film directed by
Vladimir Grammatikov, and starring Christopher Lee, Christian Bale, Nicholas Pickard, Timothy Bottoms and Susannah York.

12
00:51:39,130 --> 00:51:45,130
Based on the 1954 novel Mio, My Son by Astrid Lindgren, it tells the story of a boy from Stockholm who
travels to an otherworldly fantasy realm and frees the land from an evil knight's oppression.

13
00:55:57,391 --> 00:56:03,391
Mio in the Land of Faraway was co-produced by companies from Sweden, Norway and the Soviet Union with a budget of about fifty
million Swedish kronor, making it the most expensive film adaptation of an Astrid Lindgren book during her lifetime.

14
01:00:15,652 --> 01:00:21,652
It featured an international cast consisting largely of British, Russian and Scandinavian
actors, while its filming locations included Stockholm, Moscow, Crimea, and Scotland.

15
01:04:33,913 --> 01:04:39,913
The film was shot in English and subsequently dubbed in Swedish and Russian.

16
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
Its special effects were created by Derek Meddings.

17
01:13:10,434 --> 01:13:16,434
The film's theme song, "Mio My Mio", was composed by two former ABBA members, Benny
Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus, and performed by the Swedish band Gemini.

18
01:17:28,695 --> 01:17:34,695
Released in 1987, the film saw Nicholas Pickard's debut as an actor and
marked Christian Bale's first appearance in a feature film.

19
01:21:46,956 --> 01:21:52,956
It won the Cinekid Film Award in Amsterdam, while its
theme song became a top three hit in Sweden.

20
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
In contrast, Swedish reviewers received the film unfavorably,
criticizing it as a poor adaptation of Lindgren's novel.

21
01:30:23,478 --> 01:30:29,478
The film explores themes of friendship, prince, knight, orphan.

22
01:34:41,739 --> 01:34:47,739
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
